-- the C for an entry: the entry's own definition (for its number and type), the definitions it
-- names, held as calls, and the entry as code of the source term. A definition's own code is the
-- quote of its value, every callee unfolded and nothing shared, so an entry is always given this way
nk-emit-entry : Word → Lst Word → Code → List Word
nk-emit-entry m holds c = ce-prog-a m (x-erase m (x-forms-all (snd (program-of-at unfold m (fst (specialize (opt-or (def-type-code m) cword) (sched #64 lnil holds) lnil c)) #256))))
